This is an original automation script. It installs and orchestrates the following
third-party open-source software, each under its own license (all credit to their
respective authors):

  Rancher RKE2            Apache-2.0   https://github.com/rancher/rke2
   incl. containerd, CoreDNS, Calico/Flannel (canal), ingress-nginx,
   metrics-server                     all Apache-2.0
  Helm                    Apache-2.0   https://github.com/helm/helm
  local-path-provisioner  Apache-2.0   https://github.com/rancher/local-path-provisioner
  system-upgrade-controller Apache-2.0 https://github.com/rancher/system-upgrade-controller
  Velero                  Apache-2.0   https://github.com/vmware-tanzu/velero
  Fluent Bit              Apache-2.0   https://github.com/fluent/fluent-bit
  kube-prometheus-stack   Apache-2.0   https://github.com/prometheus-community/helm-charts

When the `save`/`push` modes build an air-gap bundle or push to a registry, they
redistribute the RKE2 binary and image tarballs (Apache-2.0 — retain copyright and
any bundled NOTICE files). The optional monitoring path (`install monitoring`)
deploys kube-prometheus-stack, which pulls **Grafana (AGPL-3.0)**; if a bundle
includes the Grafana image, also provide the corresponding source or a written
offer per the AGPL (the AGPL §13 network clause applies only if Grafana is
modified — unmodified upstream images do not trigger it).
